        "title": "Cap Codex session display when weekly quota is exhausted",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- When Codex's weekly lane is exhausted (binding cap), `CodexConsumerProjection` now shows the session lane as **0% remaining** and uses the **weekly reset time** instead of a misleading 99% / 5-hour countdown.\n- Aligns menu card, menu bar, icon, and widget usage rows with the existing burn-down widget semantics (`secondaryGloballyCapsPrimary`).\n- Adds regression tests and screenshots documenting the upstream Codex UI mismatch.\n\n### Upstream Codex UI (misleading)\n\n![Codex settings still show 99% on the 5-hour limit while weekly is 0%](https://github.com/Yuxin-Qiao/CodexBar/blob/fix/codex-weekly-caps-session-display/docs/screenshots/codex-upstream-weekly-exhausted-session-misleading.png?raw=true)\n\n### CodexBar after this fix\n\n![CodexBar session row capped to 0% with weekly reset time](https://github.com/Yuxin-Qiao/CodexBar/blob/fix/codex-weekly-caps-session-display/docs/screenshots/codexbar-weekly-caps-session-fix.png?raw=true)\n\nUpstream report: [openai/codex#31214](https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/31214)\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `swift test --filter CodexConsumerProjectionTests`\n- [x] `make check`",
